    "result_text": "Full suite passes: **263 tests, 0 failures**.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented optional, unique owner email on `POST /api/owners`:\n\n1. **API contract** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added an optional `email` string property to the `OwnerFields` schema, so it's part of both the request (`OwnerFieldsDto`) and response (`OwnerDto`). MapStruct maps it automatically by name.\n\n2. **Entity** (`Owner.java`) \u2014 added a nullable `email` column with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Database schemas** \u2014 added the `email` column to the `owners` table in all four dialects (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres). Because the hsqldb `data.sql` seed used positional `INSERT ... VALUES`, I converted those owner inserts to explicit column lists so the new nullable column doesn't break seeding (h2/postgres already used column lists).\n\n4. **Uniqueness rule** \u2014 new function `EnsureOwnerEmailUnique` that skips when no email is given, otherwise throws the existing checked `OwnerAlreadyExistsException` (\u2192 409) if another owner already uses that email. Wired it into `owners.POST.yml` as a governed step between the telephone-uniqueness check and save.\n\nThe three `Cp04Tests` (reject duplicate email, allow missing email, store and return email) pass, and no existing tests regressed.",
